### Displaying Error Messages with Column Info

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/component/Error_handling.markdown

Check for column information availability before retrieving precise error locations. The source code is required to get column details.

```php
if ($e->hasColumnInfo()) {
    echo $e->getRawMessage() . ' from ' . $e->getStartLine() . ':' . $e->getStartColumn($code)
        . ' to ' . $e->getEndLine() . ':' . $e->getEndColumn($code);
    // or:
    echo $e->getMessageWithColumnInfo($code);
} else {
    echo $e->getMessage();
}
```

--------------------------------

### Connect Sibling Nodes with NodeConnectingVisitor

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/component/FAQ.markdown

Use NodeConnectingVisitor to add parent, previous, and next sibling references to AST nodes. This visitor includes the functionality of ParentConnectingVisitor. Do not use both visitors simultaneously.

```php
use PhpParser\NodeTraverser;
use PhpParser\NodeVisitor\NodeConnectingVisitor;
use PhpParser\ParserFactory;

$code = '...';

$traverser = new NodeTraverser(new NodeConnectingVisitor);

$parser = (new ParserFactory())->createForHostVersion();
$ast    = $parser->parse($code);
$ast    = $traverser->traverse($ast);
```

--------------------------------

### Traverse AST with Token Information

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/component/Lexer.markdown

This visitor class demonstrates how to set and use token information during AST traversal. It calls the `isDeclaredUsingVar` function for property nodes and prints the result. Ensure the parser is configured to provide tokens.

```php
class MyNodeVisitor extends PhpParser\NodeVisitorAbstract {
    private $tokens;
    public function setTokens(array $tokens) {
        $this->tokens = $tokens;
    }

    public function leaveNode(PhpParser\Node $node) {
        if ($node instanceof PhpParser\Node\Stmt\Property) {
            var_dump(isDeclaredUsingVar($this->tokens, $node));
        }
    }
}
```

```php
$parser = (new PhpParser\ParserFactory())->createForHostVersion($lexerOptions);

$visitor = new MyNodeVisitor();
$traverser = new PhpParser\NodeTraverser($visitor);

try {
    $stmts = $parser->parse($code);
    $visitor->setTokens($parser->getTokens());
    $stmts = $traverser->traverse($stmts);
} catch (PhpParser\Error $e) {
    echo 'Parse Error: ', $e->getMessage();
}
```

### Lexer > Tokens, positions and attributes

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/component/Lexer.markdown

Nodes in the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) produced by the parser are mapped to ranges of tokens. The parser adds positioning attributes to AST nodes, including startLine, endLine, startTokenPos, endTokenPos, startFilePos, and endFilePos, to allow mapping nodes back to their original source code locations. These ranges are closed, meaning start and end refer to inclusive boundaries.

--------------------------------

### Usage of basic components

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/2_Usage_of_basic_components.markdown

By default, the parser automatically adds attributes like `startLine`, `endLine`, `startTokenPos`, `endTokenPos`, `startFilePos`, `endFilePos`, and `comments` to nodes. These pre-defined attributes can also be accessed through specific getter methods like `getStartLine()`.

